        "name": "USN-7000-2",
        "description": "USN-7000-1 fixed vulnerabilities in Expat. This update provides the corresponding updates for Ubuntu 22.04 LTS.  Original advisory details:   Shang-Hung Wan discovered that Expat did not properly handle certain  function calls when a negative input length was provided. An attacker  could use this issue to cause a denial of service or possibly execute  arbitrary code. (CVE-2024-45490)    Shang-Hung Wan discovered that Expat did not properly handle the  potential for an integer overflow on 32-bit platforms. An attacker  could use this issue to cause a denial of service or possibly execute  arbitrary code. (CVE-2024-45491, CVE-2024-45492)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2024-45490",
          "CVE-2024-45491",
          "CVE-2024-45492"
        ]
      },
